  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rLocation, Block, Floor and Elevation Plans- EFP/24079 - 1 \rHighways Proforma\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen/dining room shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The development shall not be occupied until details of and appropriate layout for the 6 long-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. These details should demonstrate: \rLocation: Near entrances or main access, \rDesign: Sheffield stands \rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit, \rFully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof, \rAccessibility: 1.2m wide, Step-free, no obstructions. \r\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the details stated above prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to conform to Enfield DMD policy 45 and promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to be provided within the development, together with details of bin collection access in accordance with the Enfield Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance at New Developments, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details before the development is occupied or use commences and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The development and future residents of the development will be exempt from obtaining parking permits for current and future controlled parking zones, unless they are a holder of a Blue Badge or any future equivalent. This will be secured by way of a Unilateral Undertaking, which is enforceable not only against the owner who signs the agreement but also future owners / occupants. \r\rReason: To ensure the development conforms with Enfield DMD Policy 45 paragraph 4.\r"
  ],
